    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38022" root="لهب" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهَبٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهْبٌ</span></b>  (K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهِيبٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُهَابٌ</span></b> 
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهَبَانٌ</span></b>  (S, K), [inf. ns., of which the verb,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهِبَ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهَبَ</span></b> , does not appear to have been used
in the classical ages,] The <i>flaming,</i> or <i>blazing,</i> of
fire: (S:) or its <i>flaming,</i> or <i>blazing, free from
smoke:</i> (T, K:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهَبٌ</span> signifies the <i>flame,</i> or
<i>blaze,</i> of fire: (S, K:) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهِيبٌ</span></b> , its <i>heat.</i>
(K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهَبٌ</span> <i>Dust rising</i> (K) <i>like smoke.</i> (TA.)

